{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"GHSA-464q-cqxq-xhgr","published":"2026-03-23T06:30:29Z","modified":"2026-03-30T19:56:21.371329Z","aliases":["CVE-2026-4603"],"summary":"jsrsasign: Division by Zero Allows Invalid JWK Modulus to Cause Deterministic Zero Output in RSA Operations","details":"Versions of the package jsrsasign before 11.1.1 are vulnerable to Division by zero due to the RSASetPublic/KEYUTIL parsing path in ext/rsa.js and the BigInteger.modPowInt reduction logic in ext/jsbn.js. An attacker can force RSA public-key operations (e.g., verify and encryption) to collapse to deterministic zero outputs and hide “invalid key” errors by supplying a JWK whose modulus decodes to zero.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"jsrsasign","ecosystem":"npm","purl":"pkg:npm/jsrsasign"},"ranges":[{"type":"SEMVER","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"11.1.1"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/advisories/github-reviewed/2026/03/GHSA-464q-cqxq-xhgr/GHSA-464q-cqxq-xhgr.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-4603"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/kjur/jsrsasign/pull/649"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/kjur/jsrsasign/commit/dc41d49fac4297e7a737a3ef8ebd0aa9c49ef93f"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://gist.github.com/Kr0emer/5366b7364c4fbf7e754bc377f321e9f3"},{"type":"PACKAGE","url":"https://github.com/kjur/jsrsasign"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://security.snyk.io/vuln/SNYK-JS-JSRSASIGN-15371176"}],"database_specific":{"cwe_ids":["CWE-369"],"github_reviewed":true,"github_reviewed_at":"2026-03-30T19:30:16Z","nvd_published_at":"2026-03-23T06:16:22Z","severity":"LOW"},"severity":[{"type":"CVSS_V3","score":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L"},{"type":"CVSS_V4","score":"CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N/E:P"}]}